WEBVTT

01:41.810 --> 01:49.020
[Genius Girlfriend]

01:49.370 --> 01:51.800
[Episode 3]

01:56.310 --> 01:59.120
"From the abrupt to the disordered..."

02:00.340 --> 02:02.750
[Constantly Strive to Become Stronger;
Strive to Be Number One]

02:09.080 --> 02:11.240
Duan Qiyan, seriously?
You're reading philosophy?

02:11.240 --> 02:12.700
Do you even understand it?

02:13.360 --> 02:15.220
Tang, can you just leave me alone?

02:16.230 --> 02:17.840
I'm much better than you.

02:17.770 --> 02:19.650
[Natural Philosophy]

02:18.030 --> 02:20.690
I refuse to be looked down
upon by a fool like you.

02:21.360 --> 02:23.090
This has nothing to do with grades.

02:23.090 --> 02:24.910
It's mainly about one's aura.

02:25.190 --> 02:26.800
And with your rough aura,

02:26.800 --> 02:28.150
you're only fit to read something like

02:27.270 --> 02:27.680
[Natural Philosophy]

02:28.150 --> 02:29.910
immortal cultivation
or martial arts novels.

02:29.910 --> 02:32.000
Me? Rough?

02:32.750 --> 02:34.780
Hey, I've finished The Little Prince.

02:34.780 --> 02:35.440
Here you go.

02:37.800 --> 02:38.579
I was wrong.

02:38.910 --> 02:39.910
You're not rough.

02:40.150 --> 02:42.740
You're just too immature, little prince.

02:44.560 --> 02:45.430
Let me tell you—

02:44.620 --> 02:47.980
[The Little Prince]

02:45.430 --> 02:46.630
the romance of The Little Prince

02:46.630 --> 02:48.890
is something you will never understand.

02:49.210 --> 02:50.210
Don't just laugh.

02:50.680 --> 02:52.079
What kind of book did you put
in the reading corner?

02:52.079 --> 02:52.940
I'd like to see.

02:53.650 --> 02:54.210
Guys,

02:54.210 --> 02:55.340
[Class Challenge Leaderboard]

02:54.360 --> 02:56.090
who took Tang Tingting's book?

02:57.970 --> 02:58.680
I have it.

03:00.520 --> 03:01.180
Let me see.

03:02.900 --> 03:03.970
[Constantly Strive to Become Stronger;
Strive to Be Number One]

03:04.310 --> 03:07.150
The CEO's Private Sweetheart.

03:09.410 --> 03:10.400
Typical Tang Tingting.

03:10.250 --> 03:11.350
[Class Challenge Leaderboard]

03:10.400 --> 03:11.560
This looks just like your kind of book—

03:11.560 --> 03:14.190
shallow and a total waste of time.

03:14.470 --> 03:15.630
What do you know?

03:16.400 --> 03:18.400
Web romance is also
a type of modern literature.

03:18.400 --> 03:19.470
Don't talk nonsense
if you don't understand.

03:19.470 --> 03:20.840
Fine, then let me see for myself.

03:20.030 --> 03:21.930
[The CEO's Private Sweetheart]

03:22.360 --> 03:23.840
Let me read this out loud for you guys.

03:23.840 --> 03:26.400
Mr. Dai shouted, "Come here and sit down!"

03:26.840 --> 03:28.310
His voice startled Shen Meng.

03:28.310 --> 03:30.780
Seeing that Shen Meng did not comply,
Mr. Dai pressed her step by step.

03:30.780 --> 03:32.000
He whispered in her ear...

03:32.000 --> 03:32.520
Give it to me!

03:32.520 --> 03:33.470
"Why are you hiding?"

03:33.470 --> 03:34.710
"The second button of my shirt...

03:34.710 --> 03:37.430
-Stop reading!
-fits right into your fluttering eyelashes."

03:37.430 --> 03:38.160
Give it to me!

03:39.360 --> 03:40.590
What are you doing? Don't hit me.

03:40.590 --> 03:41.310
Let's talk this out.

03:41.310 --> 03:42.630
Don't hit me! Stop!

03:44.360 --> 03:45.360
What are you doing?

03:45.360 --> 03:46.130
Don't hit me!

03:48.250 --> 03:48.860
Guys,

03:49.210 --> 03:51.120
I finished reading
The Solitude of Prime Numbers.

03:50.280 --> 03:50.840
[The Solitude of Prime Numbers]

03:51.520 --> 03:52.620
But there's no name on it.

03:52.600 --> 03:53.440
[The Solitude of Prime Numbers]

03:53.000 --> 03:53.660
Whose is it?

03:54.650 --> 03:55.150
Mine.

04:01.560 --> 04:04.830
[Gödel, Escher, Bach: an Eternal Golden Braid]

04:05.250 --> 04:06.780
How come you have this book?

04:11.180 --> 04:12.500
When I went to get the book,

04:12.500 --> 04:14.500
it was the last one left on the shelf.

04:14.930 --> 04:16.560
Although it is a bit challenging to read,

04:16.560 --> 04:18.490
I actually quite like its content.

04:18.620 --> 04:20.540
I guess I was meant to read it.

04:27.690 --> 04:29.890
[Reading Corner]

04:35.680 --> 04:38.010
So you didn't leave after school that day.

04:38.890 --> 04:39.360
What?

04:42.740 --> 04:43.540
It's nothing.

04:52.770 --> 04:54.100
I bombed the test today.

04:54.180 --> 04:55.870
I got a math question wrong
in the fill-in-the-blank section,

04:55.870 --> 04:57.270
and only scored 118.

04:58.190 --> 04:59.520
But my parents said that

04:59.690 --> 05:02.060
not getting a perfect score
means it's a total failure,

05:02.060 --> 05:03.590
they even called me a loser.

05:04.180 --> 05:05.640
But I really tried my best.

05:05.860 --> 05:07.920
I'm so tired. I really want to escape.

05:08.370 --> 05:09.680
But where can I go?

05:19.980 --> 05:20.640
Jin Baihui.

05:23.980 --> 05:25.390
I finished reading your book.

05:25.390 --> 05:26.120
It was great.

05:27.100 --> 05:30.010
I noticed some annotations inside—
I assume they're yours.

05:30.010 --> 05:31.070
I really like them.

05:36.330 --> 05:37.980
In 1915, Emmy Noether

05:37.980 --> 05:39.300
developed Noether's theorem.

05:39.300 --> 05:40.560
She has a famous quote:

05:41.120 --> 05:42.320
"Mathematics is free

05:43.159 --> 05:45.420
and unrestrained by the outside world."

05:46.659 --> 05:48.590
What exactly are you trying to say?

05:50.370 --> 05:51.180
I mean,

05:51.770 --> 05:54.130
the essence of learning is exploration.

05:54.510 --> 05:55.840
And exploration is fun.

05:56.010 --> 05:57.060
I hope you can discover

05:57.060 --> 05:58.060
the joy in it.

05:59.740 --> 06:01.940
Don't put so much pressure on yourself.

06:05.040 --> 06:05.660
[The Kite Runner]

06:07.770 --> 06:09.500
You're just talking nonsense.

06:21.300 --> 06:23.100
Did you come here just to pity me?

06:24.120 --> 06:24.510
I didn't.

06:24.510 --> 06:26.040
Who needs your pity anyway?

06:26.500 --> 06:27.430
What do you know?

06:28.000 --> 06:28.930
Do you really think a few comforting words

06:28.930 --> 06:30.190
can solve my problems?

06:30.810 --> 06:32.010
Stop acting so smart.

06:43.270 --> 06:44.000
Lin Zhixia.

06:45.330 --> 06:46.260
Don't be so smug.

06:46.860 --> 06:48.990
I will surpass you. I definitely will!

07:07.480 --> 07:10.610
Are you still upset about
what happened with Jin Baihui?

07:11.040 --> 07:12.720
I'm reflecting on my experiences

07:12.720 --> 07:14.380
and trying to learn from them.

07:14.620 --> 07:16.720
I think I really need to work on my EQ.

07:18.040 --> 07:18.770
Jiang Yubai,

07:18.860 --> 07:20.240
let me know directly

07:20.240 --> 07:21.270
if you find any issues with me,

07:21.270 --> 07:22.530
and I'll correct them.

07:26.040 --> 07:27.130
There's no need for that.

07:27.130 --> 07:27.740
Why?

07:28.130 --> 07:29.590
Just keep being yourself.

07:29.980 --> 07:31.600
Once people get to know you better,

07:31.600 --> 07:32.920
they'll all grow to like you.

07:32.920 --> 07:33.720
Liar.

07:34.240 --> 07:37.000
Since I was a kid, you're the only one
who has ever felt that way.

07:37.000 --> 07:38.420
I really want to fix this.

07:39.060 --> 07:40.860
Just tell me what the problem is.

07:41.600 --> 07:43.159
Is it because I'm too blunt?

07:47.750 --> 07:48.610
So it really is!

07:50.159 --> 07:52.450
Your expression says I'm too blunt.

07:53.800 --> 07:54.450
No.

07:59.170 --> 08:01.310
Don't tell me I've said something

08:01.310 --> 08:03.710
that accidentally hurt your feelings too?

08:07.270 --> 08:08.310
When I was seven,

08:08.310 --> 08:09.970
my mom took me to get an IQ test.

08:10.240 --> 08:12.370
It was a free test
at the City Central Hospital.

08:12.370 --> 08:14.480
My IQ was 174 back then.

08:14.920 --> 08:17.520
The doctor said
the number would keep going up.

08:17.870 --> 08:20.070
Jiang Yubai, what's your IQ?

08:20.160 --> 08:21.490
Are you smarter than me?

08:24.310 --> 08:25.010
No.

08:25.570 --> 08:27.030
I wasn't that petty, was I?

08:31.630 --> 08:34.480
Your expression clearly says
I did hurt your feelings.

08:34.480 --> 08:35.100
Maybe,

08:36.220 --> 08:37.460
occasionally.

08:38.130 --> 08:40.390
But I actually don't remember much of it.

08:40.510 --> 08:42.200
We are such good friends now.

08:42.480 --> 08:43.669
Just say what's on your mind.

08:43.669 --> 08:44.820
Don't make me guess.

08:55.150 --> 08:55.880
For example,

08:56.910 --> 08:58.920
the first semester of fourth grade...

08:58.920 --> 09:01.650
You still remember something
from that long ago?

09:04.720 --> 09:05.850
I remember you said,

09:05.910 --> 09:09.150
"Only Jiang Yubai would listen
to me talk about physics and math,

09:09.150 --> 09:11.550
even though he didn't understand a thing."

09:13.720 --> 09:15.270
I guess I really was out of line.

09:15.270 --> 09:18.070
And then there's your
"Human Observation Diary."

09:18.210 --> 09:18.680
[Human Observation Diary
is a preliminary review of research]

09:18.700 --> 09:19.130
[On the thinking patterns
of ordinary people.]

09:19.160 --> 09:19.770
[By observing the author's deskmate,
Jiang Yubai,]

09:19.630 --> 09:20.770
You want to study me

09:19.790 --> 09:20.240
[And his cognitive limitations,
this paper further explores

09:20.270 --> 09:20.820
[The thinking patterns of ordinary people]

09:21.250 --> 09:22.120
just because

09:22.500 --> 09:23.800
I'm an ordinary human?

09:24.010 --> 09:24.480
Yeah.

09:27.980 --> 09:29.310
And you even wrote in it,

09:29.670 --> 09:30.840
"I found out that Jiang Yubai

09:30.840 --> 09:33.840
knows nothing about
the famous General Relativity."

09:34.320 --> 09:36.100
I thought you said you barely remembered?

09:36.100 --> 09:38.840
How come you're reciting all this
like it was yesterday?

09:38.840 --> 09:41.040
Fine, I'll keep that in mind from now on.

09:41.340 --> 09:43.050
I feel like half of my competitive streak

09:43.050 --> 09:44.890
was shaped by you.

09:46.880 --> 09:48.410
I will admit my mistakes and correct them.

09:48.410 --> 09:49.750
I'm apologizing to you right now.

09:49.750 --> 09:51.410
Jiang Yubai is not an ordinary human—

09:51.410 --> 09:53.870
he's a great genius.

09:55.580 --> 09:56.100
No need.

09:56.750 --> 09:58.330
I'll prove it with my own ability.

09:58.330 --> 09:59.790
Okay, genius Jiang Yubai.

10:02.350 --> 10:04.150
I shouldn't have told you this
in the first place.

10:04.150 --> 10:04.680
Let's go.

10:04.860 --> 10:06.120
Yes, King Jiang Yubai.

10:06.600 --> 10:07.200
Let's go.

10:19.700 --> 10:22.460
I'll just take another
two minutes of your recess.

10:22.460 --> 10:23.250
At the end of this month,

10:23.250 --> 10:26.130
the province-wide
Rising Star Math Competition

10:26.650 --> 10:28.100
will be held in the city.

10:28.720 --> 10:29.580
This competition

10:29.580 --> 10:31.270
is a three-member team event.

10:31.740 --> 10:32.980
So if you are interested,

10:32.980 --> 10:34.820
you can form your own teams to sign up.

10:34.820 --> 10:37.370
Please hand in your registration forms
to me before next Friday.

10:37.370 --> 10:37.790
Okay?

10:38.860 --> 10:39.240
Here.

10:40.360 --> 10:41.160
Pass these on.

10:41.750 --> 10:42.750
Class dismissed.

11:01.480 --> 11:02.210
Jiang Yubai,

11:03.030 --> 11:04.340
about that math competition just now,

11:04.340 --> 11:05.940
do you want to team up with me?

11:06.000 --> 11:07.530
Are you participating too?

11:07.770 --> 11:09.010
Then the three of us can team up.

11:09.010 --> 11:10.270
That makes a full team!

11:13.130 --> 11:13.860
Jiang Yubai,

11:14.820 --> 11:17.220
I was asking if you wanted
to team up with me.

11:25.370 --> 11:27.580
The Three Departments
and Six Ministries system

11:27.580 --> 11:28.580
was the core of
the central bureaucratic system

11:28.580 --> 11:30.910
from the Sui and Tang
to the Song and the Yuan.

11:30.910 --> 11:33.860
It marked the maturity of
the ancient Chinese bureaucratic system.

11:33.860 --> 11:35.390
It divided
the central administrative organs

11:35.390 --> 11:39.210
into three major systems:
decision-making, review, and execution.

11:39.210 --> 11:41.070
Teaming up with Jiang Yubai means

11:41.150 --> 11:43.350
the math competition is a piece of cake.

11:44.100 --> 11:46.960
We're already
a sufficient condition for victory.

11:48.530 --> 11:49.620
But before the competition,

11:49.620 --> 11:52.980
I need to help him go over
the probability problems one more time.

11:52.980 --> 11:55.180
He always gets stuck on Bayes' theorem.

12:09.340 --> 12:11.500
I've made a pre-competition schedule.

12:11.500 --> 12:12.700
If we follow this plan,

12:12.700 --> 12:14.630
we can definitely get first place.

12:20.000 --> 12:20.670
Lin Zhixia.

12:22.340 --> 12:23.670
I can't team up with you.

12:33.510 --> 12:34.240
Jiang Yubai.

12:36.000 --> 12:37.260
Come here for a second.

12:41.400 --> 12:42.740
Why won't you team up with me

12:42.740 --> 12:44.000
for this competition?

12:45.170 --> 12:45.840
Lin Zhixia.

12:47.170 --> 12:48.580
As long as we team up,

12:48.720 --> 12:50.600
there will be no suspense
in this competition.

12:50.600 --> 12:52.360
Or rather, as long as you're in it,

12:52.360 --> 12:54.250
there won't be much suspense
in this competition.

12:54.250 --> 12:56.650
Because you've always been in first place.

12:57.580 --> 12:58.320
To be honest,

12:59.270 --> 13:01.740
you really are the most
capable person I've ever met.

13:01.740 --> 13:03.700
Wouldn't it be nice
to win first place with me?

13:03.700 --> 13:04.620
That would be nice.

13:04.620 --> 13:06.720
It's just that
I don't want to rely on you to win.

13:06.720 --> 13:09.580
More than that, I don't want to
just be the genius's teammate.

13:09.580 --> 13:11.720
I also want to see how big
the gap between us really is

13:11.720 --> 13:13.720
when we compete against each other.

13:21.480 --> 13:22.340
All right then.

13:22.890 --> 13:24.290
I accept your challenge.

13:25.670 --> 13:26.600
Let's make a bet.

13:27.650 --> 13:28.170
A bet?

13:31.620 --> 13:32.600
Let's make a bet.

13:33.170 --> 13:35.770
Jiang Yubai,
if you get first place in our grade,

13:35.770 --> 13:37.370
then I'll call you Mr. Jiang.

13:37.500 --> 13:39.100
But if I get first place,

13:39.170 --> 13:41.620
then you should call me
Ms. Lin to show your respect.

13:41.620 --> 13:42.480
How about that?

13:45.860 --> 13:47.270
Ms. Lin.

13:48.250 --> 13:49.980
What? What did you just call me?

13:52.370 --> 13:54.200
Ms. Lin.

13:57.410 --> 13:59.410
You want me to call you Ms. Lin again?

14:00.500 --> 14:02.500
So you still remember, Jiang Yubai.

14:02.750 --> 14:03.950
Of course I remember.

14:04.790 --> 14:06.390
That's my childhood trauma.

14:06.580 --> 14:07.780
Then I'm sorry to say,

14:07.860 --> 14:10.520
you're going
to have "childhood trauma" again.

14:10.980 --> 14:11.740
If you lose,

14:12.010 --> 14:14.390
you have to buy me
strawberry milk for a month

14:14.390 --> 14:16.720
as compensation for my emotional distress.

14:16.720 --> 14:17.700
I lose,

14:18.010 --> 14:19.940
and I still have to compensate you?

14:20.550 --> 14:21.240
Of course.

14:22.050 --> 14:22.910
Because of you,

14:23.530 --> 14:25.220
I missed out on the chance

14:25.220 --> 14:27.650
of participating in a competition
with a good friend.

14:27.650 --> 14:29.740
Don't you think you owe me that much?

14:31.260 --> 14:32.390
But what if I win?

14:33.100 --> 14:33.700
You win?

14:41.240 --> 14:43.300
I never thought about that scenario.

15:02.290 --> 15:03.890
Just say what you want to say.

15:11.860 --> 15:12.940
Do you know about

15:13.460 --> 15:16.260
the province-wide
Rising Star Math Competition?

15:17.120 --> 15:17.620
I know.

15:17.960 --> 15:18.960
I signed up for it.

15:19.700 --> 15:21.300
I need to pick two teammates.

15:21.870 --> 15:22.890
They don't have to be from my class—

15:22.890 --> 15:24.870
sophomores or seniors are all fine.

15:24.870 --> 15:26.930
Can you join the competition with me?

15:27.620 --> 15:29.250
My older brother is my student.

15:29.250 --> 15:32.050
My older brother is my student!

15:33.050 --> 15:33.980
Call me Teacher.

15:34.170 --> 15:36.230
-Call her Teacher.
-Call me Teacher.

15:36.370 --> 15:38.430
-Call her Teacher.
-Call me Teacher.

15:39.980 --> 15:40.840
Sorry, I can't.

15:44.390 --> 15:45.790
Zeqiu.

15:46.510 --> 15:48.200
I'm sincerely inviting you.

15:48.740 --> 15:50.010
Can you...

15:50.320 --> 15:51.050
No, I can't.

15:57.080 --> 15:59.210
You look ridiculous when you act cute.

16:01.720 --> 16:03.580
I'm full. Figure it out yourself.

16:11.970 --> 16:14.500
I'm really optimistic
about this Paul George card.

16:14.500 --> 16:17.560
This card's value
is definitely going up in the future.

16:17.670 --> 16:18.630
How about mine?

16:18.790 --> 16:19.620
Cousins.

16:20.050 --> 16:22.870
I went through a lot of trouble
to get it from my older brother.

16:22.870 --> 16:23.820
If you ask me,

16:24.360 --> 16:26.420
both of your cards are just mediocre.

16:27.270 --> 16:29.150
I'm currently looking into

16:29.150 --> 16:31.410
a limited-edition Kobe Gold Refractor.

16:33.000 --> 16:34.000
Limited edition?

16:34.670 --> 16:36.030
What are you dreaming about?

16:36.030 --> 16:38.200
That's not something
us regular high school kids can have.

16:38.200 --> 16:39.660
Don't be so quick to judge.

16:39.870 --> 16:41.330
To be honest with you guys,

16:41.630 --> 16:44.030
I'm about to get one.

16:45.390 --> 16:46.120
Give it to me!

16:47.000 --> 16:48.460
How are you going to get it?

16:48.630 --> 16:50.530
Don't ask, just wait and see.

16:50.980 --> 16:51.720
Let me see.

16:52.480 --> 16:53.150
Let me see.

16:53.150 --> 16:54.050
Be careful.

16:54.050 --> 16:54.580
I'm fine.

16:57.270 --> 16:58.000
Wan Chunlei.

16:58.320 --> 17:00.650
I've signed up for
the Rising Star Math Competition.

17:00.650 --> 17:02.440
Would you like to team up with me?

17:02.440 --> 17:05.440
No, thanks.
I've already teamed up with someone else.

17:08.640 --> 17:09.569
Hey, hear me out.

17:10.440 --> 17:11.960
Because...

17:11.960 --> 17:14.589
Duan Qiyan,
do you have a competition partner yet?

17:14.589 --> 17:16.190
Do you want to team up with me?

17:16.920 --> 17:18.440
Me? I think I'll pass.

17:18.440 --> 17:20.040
I've been quite busy lately.

17:20.640 --> 17:22.440
But your grades are really good, right?

17:22.440 --> 17:24.440
It would be such a pity if you skip it.

17:24.680 --> 17:26.440
Well, my grades are good for sure,

17:26.440 --> 17:28.109
but my ambitions lie elsewhere.

17:28.109 --> 17:28.640
Besides,

17:29.160 --> 17:30.680
I might not be in last place,

17:30.680 --> 17:32.000
but I'm definitely not
in first place either.

17:32.000 --> 17:32.750
So I'll pass.

17:33.160 --> 17:35.270
With me as your teammate, we'll be fine.

17:35.270 --> 17:37.160
Lin Zhixia, can't you take a hint?

17:37.640 --> 17:39.000
He has already rejected you several times.

17:39.000 --> 17:40.160
He doesn't want to team up with you.

17:40.160 --> 17:40.960
It's not like everyone

17:40.960 --> 17:42.160
has to participate in that competition.

17:42.160 --> 17:43.440
We're on our lunch break,

17:43.440 --> 17:46.370
and you just keep going on and on.
You're so annoying!

18:04.010 --> 18:04.640
Tang.

18:06.160 --> 18:07.640
Don't you think you're

18:07.640 --> 18:09.240
targeting her a bit too much?

18:09.460 --> 18:11.810
The three of us were way louder
than Lin Zhixia just now.

18:11.810 --> 18:13.000
Why are you only shouting at her?

18:13.000 --> 18:13.590
Shut up!

18:13.960 --> 18:15.160
You're annoying too.

18:35.140 --> 18:35.800
Lin Zhixia.

18:38.640 --> 18:39.370
Shen Fuxuan?

18:40.330 --> 18:41.830
I came specifically to find you.

18:41.830 --> 18:42.590
Find me?

18:44.700 --> 18:47.500
That book of yours in the reading corner
at the start of the semester,

18:47.500 --> 18:48.500
Gödel...

18:48.500 --> 18:49.850
Gödel, Escher, Bach:

18:49.850 --> 18:51.250
An Eternal Golden Braid.

18:51.750 --> 18:52.150
Right.

18:53.510 --> 18:55.310
That book is really hard to read.

18:55.310 --> 18:56.200
I hope one day

18:56.790 --> 18:59.030
I can fully digest it
and discuss it with you.

18:59.030 --> 18:59.630
Of course.

19:01.900 --> 19:03.500
About the math competition,

19:03.610 --> 19:05.470
have you found any teammates yet?

19:06.440 --> 19:07.140
Not yet.

19:08.500 --> 19:09.050
Then,

19:10.790 --> 19:11.850
can you count me in?

19:12.660 --> 19:13.860
Are you willing to...

19:16.030 --> 19:17.030
You're saying...

19:18.460 --> 19:19.070
Of course!

19:19.500 --> 19:21.760
But why are you willing
to team up with me?

19:23.030 --> 19:24.590
Participating in the competition with you

19:24.590 --> 19:26.250
should be quite interesting.

19:29.250 --> 19:32.180
Actually, I've known about you
for quite a long time.

19:32.380 --> 19:33.840
My mom mentioned you to me.

19:34.980 --> 19:36.290
Your mom is...

19:36.940 --> 19:37.740
Shen Zhaohua.

19:38.900 --> 19:40.430
Professor Shen is your mom?

19:40.810 --> 19:42.290
We've stayed in touch.

19:42.500 --> 19:44.300
She often asks about my studies.

19:45.460 --> 19:47.550
It's probably because
it's rare for her to meet someone

19:47.550 --> 19:48.900
as talented as you.

19:50.220 --> 19:53.080
I'm just interested
in the ocean and the starry sky,

19:53.140 --> 19:54.940
and I read some books about them.

19:55.500 --> 19:57.460
I bet you've had plenty of opportunities

19:57.460 --> 19:59.420
to be exposed to interesting things
since you were little.

19:59.420 --> 20:00.110
I...

20:00.810 --> 20:02.010
I guess it's alright.

20:03.750 --> 20:04.680
Then it's a deal.

20:05.270 --> 20:06.600
We'll team up together.

20:08.500 --> 20:09.500
Get one more teammate,

20:09.500 --> 20:11.110
and our team will be complete.

20:11.110 --> 20:12.710
I'll go find other students.

20:17.880 --> 20:18.610
Kid,

20:19.570 --> 20:20.400
regarding how to solve

20:20.400 --> 20:22.510
the local micro-turbulence
in the aquarium,

20:22.510 --> 20:23.790
do you have any ideas?

20:24.330 --> 20:26.330
I think we can install
artificial coral reefs.

20:26.330 --> 20:28.610
When micro-turbulence passes
through the reefs,

20:28.610 --> 20:30.610
it breaks down into milder water currents,

20:30.610 --> 20:32.470
reducing its destructive force.

20:53.200 --> 20:53.800
Excuse me,

20:55.530 --> 20:58.330
do you want to participate
in the math competition?

20:58.330 --> 20:59.060
No, we don't.

20:59.110 --> 21:00.440
We are not capable of that.

21:00.440 --> 21:01.570
Sorry to bother you.

21:07.240 --> 21:07.840
Excuse me,

21:08.380 --> 21:10.920
does either of you want
to participate in the math competition?

21:10.920 --> 21:12.050
No, we don't.

21:35.480 --> 21:37.480
Jiang Yubai, we are preparing
for the competition.

21:37.480 --> 21:39.210
Can you stop being distracted?

21:40.440 --> 21:42.240
If Lin Zhixia can't find teammates,

21:42.240 --> 21:43.750
she might not be able
to participate at all.

21:43.750 --> 21:44.810
Isn't that better?

21:45.070 --> 21:47.800
We have a better chance
of winning if she doesn't.

21:49.070 --> 21:51.600
Winning would be meaningless
if she doesn't.

21:54.570 --> 21:55.330
I mean,

21:56.510 --> 21:58.310
if Lin Zhixia doesn't participate,

21:58.310 --> 21:59.240
even if we win,

21:59.240 --> 22:01.440
other students will think we win unfairly.

22:01.440 --> 22:02.850
What's the point of a competition

22:02.850 --> 22:04.650
if the highest score is removed?

22:04.700 --> 22:06.230
This is a team competition.

22:06.380 --> 22:07.980
If she can't even form a team,

22:08.660 --> 22:09.860
she has already lost.

22:25.920 --> 22:32.880
[Death Scythe]

22:28.070 --> 22:29.600
Do you really like Han Geng?

22:29.810 --> 22:31.640
It's rare for boys to like him.

22:32.910 --> 22:35.630
[Of course, I have every album of his.]

22:35.700 --> 22:40.740
[Hey, I don't know
what kind of person you are yet.]

22:35.850 --> 22:38.220
I don't know
what kind of person you are yet.

22:38.220 --> 22:39.880
Are you handsome in real life?

22:40.760 --> 22:43.030
[Are you handsome in real life?]

22:43.030 --> 22:47.060
[Well, not bad. A little handsome.]

22:47.080 --> 22:50.880
[They all say I look like Han Geng.]

22:50.610 --> 22:52.640
Really? Do you have any photos?

22:55.070 --> 23:01.370
[I don't take photos. I'm introverted.]

23:01.290 --> 23:03.790
It doesn't matter.
We've been chatting for so long.

23:01.410 --> 23:03.710
[Well, it doesn't matter.
We've been chatting for so long.]

23:03.730 --> 23:05.860
[And we're both his fans.]

23:04.000 --> 23:05.680
And we're both his fans.

23:05.810 --> 23:08.050
Do you want to meet offline
and make friends?

23:05.880 --> 23:12.100
[Do you want to meet offline
and make friends?]

23:12.210 --> 23:16.090
[Sure.]

23:31.590 --> 23:33.550
Duan Qiyan, why are you here?

23:36.140 --> 23:37.400
I'm going to the beach.

23:39.790 --> 23:41.120
What are you doing here?

23:43.500 --> 23:44.760
None of your business.

23:46.720 --> 23:48.050
You dressed up today.

23:48.720 --> 23:49.780
Look at this dress.

23:50.720 --> 23:51.750
Are you on a date?

23:52.460 --> 23:53.200
Yes.

23:53.200 --> 23:54.900
I am on a date.

23:55.110 --> 23:55.960
The friend I am meeting later

23:55.960 --> 23:57.070
is very handsome.

23:57.070 --> 23:58.330
He looks like Han Geng.

23:59.420 --> 24:01.280
Just go. Don't get in the way here.

24:03.160 --> 24:04.660
Looks like Han Geng?

24:06.510 --> 24:07.640
Then do you think...

24:08.830 --> 24:10.110
I look like Han Geng?

24:13.070 --> 24:14.250
Angel's Tears.

24:20.500 --> 24:21.680
Duan Qiyan, I...

24:23.480 --> 24:25.160
Angel's Tears.

24:25.880 --> 24:26.830
What were you thinking?

24:26.830 --> 24:28.830
Giving yourself such a cheesy name?

24:29.640 --> 24:31.480
What does my name have to do with you?

24:31.480 --> 24:33.110
You added me out of nowhere

24:33.110 --> 24:34.240
and didn't even tell me.

24:34.240 --> 24:36.270
It's none of your business if I add you.

24:36.270 --> 24:37.110
Besides,

24:37.380 --> 24:38.510
you accepted it, didn't you?

24:38.510 --> 24:38.940
I...

24:42.180 --> 24:43.570
Wait, stop it.

24:43.880 --> 24:45.160
You have to think about it this way.

24:45.160 --> 24:46.480
At least, I was the one who added you.

24:46.480 --> 24:49.110
Think about it.
At the prime of your youth,

24:49.110 --> 24:51.570
a young girl like you
meets someone offline.

24:51.750 --> 24:53.200
What if you run into a bad guy?

24:53.200 --> 24:54.240
Meeting a liar like you

24:54.240 --> 24:57.720
-is worse than meeting a bad guy.
-Tang Tingting, let go!

24:57.920 --> 24:58.720
No, I won't.

24:58.720 --> 25:00.160
If you don't, I'll fight back.

25:00.160 --> 25:01.590
Don't you dare!

25:01.750 --> 25:03.030
Three, two, one.

25:03.180 --> 25:05.290
You... let go, Tang Tingting.

25:05.290 --> 25:06.440
You let go!

25:07.920 --> 25:10.000
Tingting, are you two playing around?

25:10.000 --> 25:10.730
Yeah, we are.

25:11.000 --> 25:12.000
Take care, Auntie Liu.

25:12.000 --> 25:13.240
Alright, have fun.

25:13.240 --> 25:13.840
Take care.

25:17.200 --> 25:18.440
Are you letting go or not?

25:18.440 --> 25:19.240
You let go.

25:19.420 --> 25:20.270
You... you...

25:20.270 --> 25:21.200
let go.

25:21.200 --> 25:22.110
You let go.

25:23.030 --> 25:24.940
Tang Tingting, let go.

25:25.200 --> 25:26.600
I won't. You let go first.

25:26.790 --> 25:27.660
If you don't,

25:28.050 --> 25:28.960
I'm going to suffocate.

25:28.960 --> 25:29.490
Hurry up.

25:29.640 --> 25:30.810
You let go first.

25:31.400 --> 25:32.270
Be gentle.

25:33.160 --> 25:33.820
Duan Qiyan.

25:35.200 --> 25:36.060
Tang Tingting!

25:36.830 --> 25:38.070
Uncle, he hit me!

25:38.550 --> 25:38.960
Dad,

25:39.510 --> 25:40.240
I didn't.

25:41.110 --> 25:41.570
Auntie,

25:42.070 --> 25:43.050
she started it.

25:46.070 --> 25:46.940
What happened?

25:47.790 --> 25:49.920
Tell me what happened.

25:50.680 --> 25:53.010
I just got back
and saw you bullying a girl.

25:54.920 --> 25:56.380
How do I usually teach you?

25:56.550 --> 25:57.880
As a gentleman,

25:58.070 --> 25:59.110
you must first...

25:59.330 --> 26:00.310
Be responsible.

26:00.310 --> 26:00.770
Then...

26:00.920 --> 26:01.590
Know how to listen,

26:01.590 --> 26:03.310
and not interrupt others casually.

26:03.310 --> 26:03.750
And?

26:03.960 --> 26:04.820
Respect women.

26:05.090 --> 26:05.640
Did you do that?

26:05.640 --> 26:06.090
No.

26:08.400 --> 26:10.550
Tingting's mom, I'm really sorry.

26:10.550 --> 26:11.590
I've failed to teach my son well.

26:11.590 --> 26:12.790
Sorry for the trouble.

26:12.790 --> 26:14.920
-Sorry. Sorry.
-Don't say that, Duan.

26:15.400 --> 26:17.500
We both know our own kids best.

26:17.740 --> 26:19.050
It takes two to tango.

26:19.440 --> 26:20.140
Yes.

26:21.590 --> 26:22.350
Don't hit the kid.

26:22.350 --> 26:24.070
You even tackled him!

26:24.070 --> 26:26.750
A girl tackled a boy?

26:26.880 --> 26:28.140
Is that how a lady acts?

26:28.270 --> 26:29.110
Exactly.

26:29.110 --> 26:29.640
Unbelievable.

26:29.640 --> 26:31.850
Auntie, you need to be the judge.

26:32.200 --> 26:33.070
Today, I was online

26:33.070 --> 26:34.800
and played a little joke on her.

26:34.850 --> 26:35.920
And she tackled me.

26:35.920 --> 26:36.750
Was that necessary?

26:36.750 --> 26:37.740
It really wasn't.

26:37.740 --> 26:38.200
Enough.

26:38.790 --> 26:40.450
You think you're in the right?

26:41.590 --> 26:42.590
Online?

26:44.310 --> 26:45.960
Weren't you doing homework at home today?

26:45.960 --> 26:47.660
When were you online?

26:48.350 --> 26:49.700
Um, Tingting's mom.

26:50.770 --> 26:52.830
If there's nothing else, we'll head back.

26:52.830 --> 26:54.590
Alright, sorry for the trouble.

26:54.590 --> 26:56.050
Please don't be so polite.

26:56.070 --> 26:57.330
-I won't see you off.
-Bye. Bye.

26:57.330 --> 26:58.140
Bye. Bye.

27:01.460 --> 27:01.980
I...

27:02.160 --> 27:03.960
I'll throw the trash out for you.

27:05.110 --> 27:05.920
So gentlemanly.

27:05.920 --> 27:07.000
See you. See you.

27:07.000 --> 27:07.920
Thanks, Duan.

27:10.830 --> 27:13.430
I'll settle the score with you
when we get home.

27:13.770 --> 27:14.900
Here, throw it away.

27:26.520 --> 27:28.860
[Points Card]

27:37.590 --> 27:38.000
Dad.

27:38.830 --> 27:39.760
Have some water.

27:41.590 --> 27:42.500
Thanks.

27:43.010 --> 27:44.420
My pleasure, Dad.

27:46.940 --> 27:47.400
Tell me.

27:48.610 --> 27:51.140
How many points
have you saved up on this card?

27:55.900 --> 27:56.610
Not many.

27:58.660 --> 27:59.290
It's fine.

27:59.500 --> 28:01.590
I can check it even if you don't tell me.

28:01.590 --> 28:03.050
I used to play too, right?

28:03.240 --> 28:04.170
I've been there.

28:04.900 --> 28:06.660
But the rule in our family

28:06.900 --> 28:10.010
is leniency for confession
and severity for resistance.

28:10.010 --> 28:11.030
You know this.

28:11.250 --> 28:12.500
So I suggest

28:12.830 --> 28:14.310
you just tell me.

28:14.940 --> 28:16.340
I promise I won't hit you.

28:18.770 --> 28:19.510
Really?

28:20.440 --> 28:21.750
Of course.

28:22.010 --> 28:22.740
Just tell me.

28:26.720 --> 28:28.480
Fifty or sixty thousand.

28:30.480 --> 28:31.880
Fifty or sixty thousand?

28:38.180 --> 28:40.160
Dad, I'll never go again!

28:40.420 --> 28:41.420
I mean it!

28:41.680 --> 28:42.240
Dad!

28:43.010 --> 28:43.460
Dad!

28:44.570 --> 28:46.170
Duan Wenming, be civilized!

28:46.270 --> 28:47.460
It's illegal to beat kids!

28:47.460 --> 28:48.000
Ouch!

28:48.220 --> 28:49.460
Ouch, it hurts!

28:53.180 --> 28:53.980
Class is over.

28:54.000 --> 28:55.640
Let's go downstairs and play basketball.

28:55.640 --> 28:56.170
Let's go.

28:57.050 --> 28:58.570
I'm covered in bruises.

28:59.500 --> 29:00.880
I think I'll skip it.

29:07.010 --> 29:09.180
It's all because of that Tang Tingting.

29:09.180 --> 29:11.310
She ruined my sports player card plan.

29:12.090 --> 29:14.570
The limited-edition Kobe card
you mentioned last time?

29:14.570 --> 29:15.270
Yes.

29:15.810 --> 29:16.570
I bet

29:16.570 --> 29:18.000
I found the only one in the whole city,

29:18.000 --> 29:19.400
right at Lele Toys"R"Us.

29:19.810 --> 29:21.720
That's their grand prize.

29:21.940 --> 29:24.000
It takes 100,000 points to redeem it.

29:24.250 --> 29:25.700
I worked hard to save up for over a week.

29:25.700 --> 29:26.900
I finally managed...

29:27.140 --> 29:28.850
to save half of the points, but...

29:28.850 --> 29:29.660
my dad

29:29.660 --> 29:31.460
snapped the points card in half.

29:39.810 --> 29:42.000
Aren't you short of a teammate right now?

29:42.000 --> 29:43.240
Duan Qiyan is now completely

29:43.240 --> 29:44.370
obsessed with this.

29:44.810 --> 29:46.380
You can start from this point

29:46.380 --> 29:47.640
and get him on the team.

29:51.250 --> 29:53.480
Arcade sports player card.

29:54.460 --> 29:55.680
That's my blind spot.

29:57.240 --> 29:59.500
I haven't really dealt with this before.

29:59.610 --> 30:01.700
But we have a short holiday coming up.

30:02.380 --> 30:03.580
Let's go check it out.

30:05.830 --> 30:08.290
I've never even seen
these machines before.

30:09.140 --> 30:10.250
Duan Qiyan tried for so long

30:10.250 --> 30:11.420
and couldn't win the grand prize.

30:11.420 --> 30:12.350
Can we do it?

30:13.250 --> 30:14.310
Let's give it a try.

30:14.460 --> 30:16.260
Duan Qiyan is just too obsessed.

30:16.550 --> 30:18.050
I think there are some tricks

30:18.050 --> 30:20.420
and patterns to these games.

30:23.590 --> 30:25.190
Sir, your tickets are saved.

30:27.250 --> 30:28.180
Okay, thank you.

30:33.140 --> 30:34.670
What are you two doing here?

30:35.110 --> 30:35.770
Duan Qiyan,

30:36.290 --> 30:37.620
how about we make a deal?

30:38.420 --> 30:39.020
What deal?

30:40.290 --> 30:42.480
If we help you redeem
the sports player card,

30:42.480 --> 30:44.720
you'll join Lin Zhixia's
math competition group.

30:44.720 --> 30:45.580
What do you say?

30:46.220 --> 30:47.680
Are you kidding me, Jiang?

30:48.250 --> 30:50.180
The sports player card
has been there for so long.

30:50.180 --> 30:52.240
Do you think you can easily redeem it?

30:57.250 --> 30:59.480
Anyway, we are confident.

31:00.010 --> 31:02.140
It just depends on whether you want it.

31:03.740 --> 31:04.220
Fine.

31:04.740 --> 31:06.770
If you can really
get me the card,

31:07.090 --> 31:08.490
forget about teaming up,

31:08.770 --> 31:10.300
I can even be your follower.

31:13.610 --> 31:14.980
These are my remaining tokens.

31:14.980 --> 31:16.050
You guys take them and play.

31:16.050 --> 31:17.570
Everything here is a scam.

31:17.640 --> 31:18.830
I've quit now.

31:19.460 --> 31:20.720
Bye-bye. I'm leaving.

31:26.420 --> 31:28.790
[Commemorative Kobe Card]

31:29.680 --> 31:31.810
Why do I suddenly feel so competitive?

31:32.610 --> 31:33.140
Me too.

31:33.850 --> 31:35.840
[Commemorative Kobe Card]

31:38.330 --> 31:40.590
Although it's my first time at an arcade,

31:40.850 --> 31:43.140
it's even more fun than I imagined.

31:44.570 --> 31:46.170
The music rising and falling

31:46.610 --> 31:47.940
and the colorful lights

31:48.400 --> 31:49.700
seemed to turn the whole world

31:49.700 --> 31:52.010
into a giant candy box.

32:02.530 --> 32:05.010
We tried all the games.

32:06.220 --> 32:08.250
The sense of accomplishment
from completing challenges together

32:08.250 --> 32:10.720
is more real and thrilling than any prize.

32:11.400 --> 32:13.680
We even forgot
our original intention while playing,

32:13.680 --> 32:16.160
which was to help Duan Qiyan
get the sports player card

32:16.160 --> 32:18.890
to make him my teammate
for the math competition.

32:25.700 --> 32:28.230
When the doll
we wanted most finally dropped,

32:29.240 --> 32:30.370
I suddenly realized

32:31.110 --> 32:33.700
my very first time at an arcade

32:34.110 --> 32:35.920
was with Jiang Yubai.

32:37.030 --> 32:39.160
It feels like whatever we do together,

32:39.400 --> 32:41.460
we're blessed with incredible luck.

32:42.530 --> 32:43.070
Perhaps,

32:44.050 --> 32:46.010
having a good friend by your side

32:47.160 --> 32:48.680
is the greatest reward

32:49.940 --> 32:50.940
bestowed by fate.

32:58.920 --> 33:00.720
Congratulations to both of you.

33:10.270 --> 33:10.670
How...

33:11.570 --> 33:12.170
did you...

33:12.880 --> 33:14.070
do that?

33:14.160 --> 33:15.250
Never mind that.

33:15.550 --> 33:17.110
According to our previous agreement,

33:17.110 --> 33:18.940
can you join my team now?

33:22.310 --> 33:24.840
Are you really going
to join the competition?

33:27.630 --> 33:28.960
Look, Lin Zhixia,

33:29.310 --> 33:30.270
I don't really

33:30.660 --> 33:33.160
like doing stressful things.

33:33.770 --> 33:36.230
So let's just forget
about the competition.

33:36.480 --> 33:37.830
Didn't we agree on this?

33:38.480 --> 33:39.750
Don't you want the card?

33:39.750 --> 33:41.250
Yes, I do want it.

33:41.680 --> 33:42.140
But

33:43.030 --> 33:45.550
let me think about the competition
a bit more.

33:45.550 --> 33:47.500
Why are you breaking your promise?

33:48.000 --> 33:50.000
I'm not breaking my promise, Jiang.

33:51.880 --> 33:53.200
Zhixia is here.

33:53.200 --> 33:55.200
-Hello, Mr. Duan.
-Long time no see.

33:56.110 --> 33:57.550
This is my classmate, Jiang Yubai.

33:57.550 --> 33:58.220
Hello, Mr. Duan.

33:58.220 --> 33:58.880
Hello.

33:59.270 --> 33:59.940
Have a seat.

33:59.940 --> 34:01.340
Make yourselves at home.

34:02.310 --> 34:04.240
You haven't visited in a long time.

34:04.310 --> 34:05.440
What do you want for dinner?

34:05.440 --> 34:06.370
I'll arrange it.

34:06.830 --> 34:08.150
We don't need to stay for dinner.

34:08.150 --> 34:09.280
I came to find Duan Qiyan

34:09.280 --> 34:11.280
to talk about the math competition.

34:11.510 --> 34:12.570
Math competition?

34:14.280 --> 34:15.610
What math competition?

34:15.840 --> 34:16.770
You didn't know?

34:17.820 --> 34:18.780
I really didn't.

34:20.760 --> 34:21.760
It's like this, Mr. Duan.

34:21.760 --> 34:23.380
This is a very important

34:23.380 --> 34:24.980
provincial math competition.

34:24.980 --> 34:27.090
The best students
in the province are participating.

34:27.090 --> 34:28.949
Because it's a team competition,

34:28.980 --> 34:31.310
most of our classmates have formed teams.

34:31.500 --> 34:33.440
But Duan Qiyan hasn't signed up yet.

34:33.440 --> 34:35.960
So we wanted to try to convince him.

34:36.320 --> 34:37.150
Just give it a try,

34:37.150 --> 34:38.750
even if the chances are slim.

34:40.630 --> 34:41.440
So you mean

34:41.440 --> 34:42.960
this kid didn't even want

34:42.960 --> 34:44.230
to participate in the math competition.

34:44.230 --> 34:45.429
Is that what you mean?

34:46.110 --> 34:47.110
No, Dad.

34:47.400 --> 34:49.050
I've been planning it.

34:49.510 --> 34:50.510
I just

34:50.510 --> 34:52.380
don't know which team to join.

34:53.230 --> 34:55.820
I take this competition very seriously.

34:56.070 --> 34:57.600
I was planning to win a prize

34:57.630 --> 34:58.890
to give you a surprise.

35:00.510 --> 35:01.640
Isn't that perfect?

35:01.840 --> 35:03.610
Lin Zhixia is the best in the school.

35:03.610 --> 35:05.470
Isn't this the best opportunity?

35:05.760 --> 35:06.560
That's right.

35:07.260 --> 35:08.920
If you can team up with Zhixia,

35:09.360 --> 35:10.690
isn't that a good thing?

35:10.730 --> 35:12.390
What were you thinking about?

35:14.670 --> 35:15.460
Sure.

35:16.010 --> 35:16.870
Then I'll join.

35:17.320 --> 35:19.850
We'll start making plans
when school starts.

35:20.150 --> 35:23.420
Secure second
and aim for first in this competition.

35:25.510 --> 35:26.800
Quite ambitious.

35:26.800 --> 35:28.400
Secure second and aim for first.

35:28.400 --> 35:28.730
Fine.

35:29.360 --> 35:31.510
Anyway, I always

35:31.510 --> 35:33.570
give clear rewards and punishments,

35:33.760 --> 35:35.800
and I always keep my word.

35:37.190 --> 35:38.590
Please help him out more.

35:39.230 --> 35:41.130
Don't just chat. Have some fruit.

35:41.320 --> 35:42.580
You guys keep talking.

35:42.710 --> 35:45.710
I'm counting on you
to secure second and aim for first.

35:55.230 --> 35:55.820
Great.

35:56.190 --> 35:57.840
With Shen Fuxuan and Duan Qiyan,

35:57.840 --> 35:59.700
my competition team is complete.

36:20.080 --> 36:27.750
♪ Wandering light wind
drifts past your pupils ♪

36:28.860 --> 36:33.090
♪ One second of encounter,
heartstrings stirred ♪

36:33.710 --> 36:37.180
♪ The story feels altogether different ♪

36:39.280 --> 36:39.900
What are you doing?

36:39.280 --> 36:47.020
♪ How to describe
my whimsical wandering dream? ♪

36:48.270 --> 36:52.490
♪ You softly answer my quirky side ♪

36:52.840 --> 36:53.960
There was a leaf on your head.

36:52.880 --> 36:56.220
♪ Such bliss to finally be understood ♪

36:57.690 --> 37:00.930
♪ The moon drifts past the window ♪

36:57.760 --> 36:58.760
What else can I do?

37:02.450 --> 37:06.030
♪ How am I to understand? ♪

37:03.130 --> 37:03.880
I mean,

37:05.150 --> 37:06.900
how did a leaf get on my head?

37:07.450 --> 37:08.490
♪ About you ♪

37:08.050 --> 37:09.530
Why did it fall on my head?

37:09.880 --> 37:14.220
♪ The moment our eyes met,
my world came alive with color ♪

37:14.890 --> 37:19.260
♪ Could this be how love begins? ♪

37:19.780 --> 37:22.760
♪ These unspoken feelings
are so hard to figure out ♪

37:20.360 --> 37:21.320
There's a formula relating wind speed V,

37:21.320 --> 37:22.710
the falling leaf's initial height H,

37:22.710 --> 37:24.820
and wind direction θ.

37:23.340 --> 37:28.740
♪ Hidden deep within your gaze ♪

37:29.060 --> 37:33.490
♪ Sometimes, I imagine
drifting beyond the skies with you ♪

37:30.780 --> 37:32.320
If even a falling leaf's trajectory

37:32.320 --> 37:34.110
can be predicted by a formula,

37:34.040 --> 37:38.060
♪ Shimmering light
dances over the flower in bloom ♪

37:35.420 --> 37:37.220
then encounters between people

37:37.500 --> 37:38.760
might also be a gentle algorithm

37:38.760 --> 37:40.550
quietly run by the universe.

37:38.880 --> 37:41.950
♪ After all we've been through,
our fates remain intertwined ♪

37:42.030 --> 37:43.570
This is both scientific certainty

37:42.630 --> 37:49.120
♪ Perhaps fate favors me now ♪

37:44.480 --> 37:46.090
and emotional coincidence.

37:47.440 --> 37:49.100
But eventually, all formulas

37:49.840 --> 37:51.980
will collapse into one true equation.

38:07.340 --> 38:11.680
♪ The moment our eyes met,
my world came alive with color ♪

38:12.350 --> 38:16.720
♪ Could this be how love begins? ♪

38:17.240 --> 38:20.220
♪ These unspoken feelings
are so hard to figure out ♪

38:20.800 --> 38:26.250
♪ Hidden deep within your gaze ♪

38:26.530 --> 38:30.960
♪ The moment our eyes met,
my world was filled with hope ♪

38:31.540 --> 38:35.900
♪ Dim tender touches turn out to be love ♪

38:36.420 --> 38:39.250
♪ Unsettling thoughts at last unfold ♪

38:39.990 --> 38:45.270
♪ I return the moment you glance back ♪

38:45.720 --> 38:49.800
♪ If reunion is fated ♪

38:50.690 --> 38:54.100
♪ Wish upon that dust speck
amid flowing light ♪
